  },
  "global_conditions": {
    "plenary": "State of grace; no attachment even to venial sin; prescribed work; sacramental confession, Eucharistic communion and prayer for the Roman Pontiff's intentions; specific concession exceptions. Generally at most one plenary per day, except point of death.",
    "partial": "At least a contrite heart and precise work and conditions; not simply owning an item or celebrating a date.",
    "for_deceased": "Applicable by way of suffrage, with specified departed-only concessions; cannot claim an individual obtained an indulgence.",
    "calendar": "A grant tied to a particular liturgical day follows its own canonical date and legitimate transfer rules; 1962 calendar presentation does not independently redefine indulgence law.",
    "historical": "Pre-1967 grants and 1962 Raccolta numbers are not presumed legally in force; particular later grants require their own decree."
  },
